#DESCRIPTION
Single-cell periodic hybrid-PIC regression test.

The domain contains exactly ONE grid cell with periodic boundary conditions in
all three directions. On a single cell there is no spatial variation, so every
finite-difference gradient -- in particular curl B -- is identically zero.
Because the Hall term of the generalized Ohm's law is (J x B)/rho with
J = curl B / (4 pi), the Hall term is EXACTLY zero here. With a uniform plasma
(zero bulk velocity) the convective term U_i x B also vanishes, so the electric
field E stays zero and the guide field B is frozen: dB/dt = -curl E = 0.

This test verifies that the hybrid solver does no spurious work when the Hall
term must vanish: the magnetic energy Eb must stay constant (to round-off) and
no NaN/blow-up may occur. It guards against a class of bugs where the Hall or
convective term is applied even on a single-cell / no-curl configuration.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-0.5                    xMin  [code units; Lx = 1]
 0.5                    xMax
-0.5                    yMin
 0.5                    yMax
-0.5                    zMin
 0.5                    zMax

#NCELL
1                       nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
1                       maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

Hall term ON (this test confirms it contributes exactly zero on a single cell).
#HALLTERM
T                       useHallTerm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); electron is implicit neutralizing fluid.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

Uniform guide field Bx0; zero bulk velocity so U_i x B = 0 too.
#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
10000.0                 T [K]
1.0439e-8               bx [T]       uniform guide field Bx0 (B_code ~ 1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = 1 s; sets cLight_SI = uNormSI

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

Particles present (so rho > 0 and the cell is "active"), but uniform => curl B = 0.
#PARTICLES
4                       nParticle per cell in X
4                       nParticle per cell in Y
4                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx
Bx By Bz Ex Ey Ez       varName

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
2.0                     TimeMax   frozen-field (curl B=0) run

#RUN
